 ### Types of Attacks

1. 🧬 Virus        
Copies itself by attaching to a file/program 
2.  🐛 Worm     
 Copies itself independently, no host needed  
3.  🐴 Trojan Horse 
 Disguised as a legit program, but harmful    
4.  🕵️ Rootkit     
 Hidden, high-level (privileged) access       
5. 👁️ Spyware     
 Secretly monitors & steals your data         
6. 📢 Adware    
Shows unwanted ads without consent           
7. 🤖 Bot       
Waits for hacker's remote commands            
8. 🔒 Ransomware    
Locks data/system until ransom is paid       
9. 😱 Scareware     
Fake warnings trick you into installing malware

  🎣 2.2 Methods of Infiltration 

Social_Engineering:
  definition: "Tricking people into revealing confidential info"
  types:
    - Phishing: "Fake emails/websites used to steal info"
    - Spear_Phishing: "Phishing targeted at ONE specific person/org"

MitM_Attacks:
  Man-in-the-Middle (MitM):
    desc: "Attacker secretly intercepts communication between two devices"
  Man-in-the-Mobile (MitMo):
    desc: "MitM but targets mobile devices, can steal 2FA/SMS codes"
    example: "ZeuS malware"




